load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A Turing machine: the foundational model of computation, a finite control reading and writing symbols on an unbounded
# tape, one step at a time, by a transition rule. What a Turing machine can compute is what is computable at all (the
# Church-Turing thesis), and the substrate's two-step rule (collide then stream over the mesh) is itself a universal
# computer of this strength. The form carries the set of states and the tape alphabet; the transition rule and the
# accept condition are the machine's program.
form turing-machine
  link states, like set
  link alphabet, like set
